  "purpose": "Prioritize global dataset publication candidates by scholarly uptake, retaining reuse and native-format checks.",
  "precommitted_rules": [
    "Use one provider, OpenAlex cited_by_count, for comparable counts; snapshot the count, resolved work ID, DOI, title and retrieval time.",
    "Match the dataset-specific recommended publication(s), not a general method, platform, unrelated application, or the GEE Community Catalog paper.",
    "Curate publication identity and geographic scope without seeing citation counts; record uncertainty and unresolved identities.",
    "Rank by the largest citation count among validated associated dataset papers; do not sum counts across papers or paper/data DOI records because citing works can overlap.",
    "Report direct dataset-DOI counts separately. Neither paper citations nor data citations prove the number of dataset users.",
    "Keep total citations as the requested ranking metric; retain publication year and recent per-year counts as context for age bias, without silently replacing the requested ranking.",
    "Missing identifiers, unindexed works, API failures and unresolved matches remain unknown, never zero. Explicit returned zero is a measured zero.",
    "Keep global, regional, mixed and unresolved geographic scope separate. Prioritize global candidates; mixed families need product-level scope review.",
    "Rank citation demand separately from publication readiness. Existing suitable native copies normally need registry coverage rather than another mirror.",
    "Resolve license, exact release, footprint, native alternatives and conversion feasibility before publishing; no GEE or cloud compute jobs in this citation survey."
  ],
